  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TB Local Organization Network-2 (TB LON-2)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Malawi):  USAID&apos;s Tuberculosis Local Organizations Network-2 (TB LON-2) activity will support the National Tuberculosis and Leprosy Elimination Program to implement its strategic plan by addressing TB programmatic gaps with locally generated solutions. TB LON-2 will use FY 2022 funds to: 1) implement an active TB case finding intervention at twenty one health facilities in three high-burden districts and link the diagnosed TB patients to effective treatment; 2) implement the TB treatment guideline on shortened, fully-oral treatment regimen for drug resistant TB; 3) improve access to timely and quality diagnosis, effective prevention, treatment, and care services for TB while reducing stigma, creating demand, and addressing patient and community TB treatment needs; 4) implement innovative strategies for contact investigation of pulmonary TB patients; 5) scale-up the use of stool-based specimen to detect TB in children; and 6) build the capacity of health facility staff and community volunteers including those from private not-for-profit facilities in TB screening, prevention, and treatment. ..TB LON-2 is aligned with the U.S. government&apos;s Global TB Strategy and the USAID&apos;s Global Accelerator business model to End TB that support the goal of reaching every person with TB, curing those in need of treatment, and preventing disease progression and new infections. TB LON-2 supports the Joint Strategic Plan Objective 1.1: Strengthen global health security, combat infectious disease threats, and address priority global health challenges through bilateral engagement and within multilateral fora. The activity also supports the Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective 3.2: Malawi improves access to and quality of health services so that more of its citizens gain and retain full health and are able to contribute productively at home, in the community, and at work.....</narrative>
  </description>
